# attack — struck with a weapon
#
# The third arm, and neither a success nor a failure of the roll: it is the tool gate. A verb struck
# with a fighting medium takes a weapon without a critic call and refuses anything else without one
# either, and the weapon then REPLACES the body — the blow is drawn from the axe's own skill list
# rather than from the hands and feet the same character would otherwise have used.
#
# The reference-tool comparison matters here: an ordinary Optional verb would put a battle axe to the
# item-use critic, which under --playground picks its verdict at random and would make this a coin
# flip. `Verb.UsesFightingMedium` is what settles it in code instead.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item battle_axe --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal attack
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

# Combining does not execute: it rewrites the action to include the weapon and offers THAT as a new
# button. Executing the reformulated one is what puts CombinedItem on the action, which is how the
# blow learns which weapon is in the hand.
click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
click action 1
choose 0

advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect SUCCESS
expect-verb attack
expect-outcome first_blow

# Chop is an axe skill and belongs to no organ medium, so its name in the chip is the proof that the
# weapon supplied the blow rather than the body. Battlecraft is the modus mentis behind it — the
# lesson follows the blow, which is the whole reason attack declares none of its own.
expect First blow: Chop
expect Modus mentis learned: Battlecraft

# And it landed on him like any other first blow.
expect-state npcs brewer alive=True affinity=Stranger enemy=False hp=4/5 wounds=1

click button
wait mode Fighting 60
quit
